# Docker Development Guidelines

## Multi-Stage Environment
- Application builds use Alpine-based multi-stage targets: `development` and `production`.
- The `app` service runs PHP-FPM and Nginx/Alpine with PHP 8.4.
- Ancillary services include `db` (MariaDB 10.11) and `redis` (Redis 7).

## Execution Guidelines
- Whenever executing PHP, Composer, Artisan, or Pint commands, execute them within the running `app` container:
  ```bash
  docker compose exec app php artisan <command>
  docker compose exec app php vendor/bin/pint --test
  ```
- If the stack is stopped, use isolated on-demand containers:
  ```bash
  docker run --rm -v $(pwd):/var/www -w /var/www php:8.4-cli php artisan test
  docker run --rm -v $(pwd):/app -w /app php:8.4-cli php vendor/bin/pint --test
  ```
- Windows developers use `docker-compose.windows.yml` (`composer windows:start`).
